    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (74.29) headlines our lineup as the premier play. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Yesavage and a massive boost from his spot in the leadoff role, paired with an elite 0.425 xwOBA that suggests he is primed to capitalize on this start. **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) also stands out as a high-upside play; he draws a soft matchup against Rodriguez, and the combination of park factors and a favorable platoon split makes him a core offensive driver today. We are also leaning heavily into the weakness of Lauer, which elevates **Josh Naylor** (66.08) and **Cole Young** (63.25) into the \"Strong\" start tier, as both capitalize on the 5.30 xERA of the opposing starter.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Edwin Arroyo**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 47.66 score. While he presents as a versatile switch-hitter, the current configuration of our middle infield\u2014featuring the table-setting speed of **Brice Turang** (60.53) and the high-floor profile of **Travis Bazzana** (52.84)\u2014pushed him to the pine. We are cognizant of the risks posed by elite catchers today; both **Corbin Carroll** (60.19) and **Austin Riley** (47.75) see minor efficiency dips due to the defensive prowess of their opponents behind the plate. While **Corbin Carroll** remains a mandatory start due to his stolen base potential, **Austin Riley** is currently operating at a marginal level and should be monitored closely if the game script shifts. Finally, with **Vinnie Pasquantino** remaining on the IL, our depth is being tested, though we are comfortable with **Tyler Soderstrom** (64.05) anchoring the outfield today given the favorable park factors in his matchup against Sandoval.",
